msgid "Implementing a custom Stork service registrar"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide explains how to implement a custom service registrar for https://"
"smallrye.io/smallrye-stork[SmallRye Stork] and use it to programmatically "
"register service instances at startup."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are new to Stork, please read the xref:stork.adoc[Stork Getting "
"Started Guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _preview_, backward compatibility and presence in the ecosystem is not "
"guaranteed.\n"
"Specific improvements might require changing configuration or APIs, and "
"plans to become _stable_ are under way.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Roughly 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK 17+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally Mandrel or GraalVM installed and xref:building-native-image."
"adoc#configuring-graalvm[configured appropriately] if you want to build a "
"native executable (or Docker if you use a native container build)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

msgid "In this guide, we will build an application that:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Implements a custom service registrar by extending Stork's SPI"
msgstr ""

msgid "Programmatically registers a service instance at startup"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configures the registrar via `application.properties`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Beyond service discovery and load balancing, it also supports xref:stork-"
"registration.adoc[_service registration_].\n"
"Service registration is the process of announcing a service instance to a "
"registry so that other services can discover it.\n"
"While Stork provides built-in registrars for Consul, Eureka, and others, you "
"can implement your own by using the Stork SPI."
msgstr ""

msgid "Solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend that you follow the instructions in the next sections and "
"create the application step by step.\n"
"However, you can go right to the completed example."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clone the Git repository: `git clone {quickstarts-clone-url}`, or download "
"an {quickstarts-archive-url}[archive]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The solution is located in the `stork-programmatic-custom-registration-"
"quickstart` link:{quickstarts-tree-url}/stork-programmatic-custom-"
"registration-quickstart[directory]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bootstrapping the project"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Create a Quarkus project importing the quarkus-rest, quarkus-smallrye-stork, "
"and quarkus-rest-client-jackson extensions using your favorite approach:"
msgstr ""

msgid "CLI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create a Gradle project, add the `--gradle` or `--gradle-kotlin-dsl` "
"option."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about how to install and use the Quarkus CLI, see the "
"xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Maven"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To create a Gradle project, add the `-DbuildTool=gradle` or `-DbuildTool="
"gradle-kotlin-dsl` option."
msgstr ""

msgid "For Windows users:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If using cmd, (don't use backward slash `\\` and put everything on the same "
"line)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If using Powershell, wrap `-D` parameters in double quotes e.g. `\"-"
"DprojectArtifactId={create-app-artifact-id}\"`"
msgstr ""

msgid "In the generated project, also add the following dependencies:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`stork-core` provides the Stork API and SPI needed to implement a custom "
"registrar.\n"
"`stork-configuration-generator` generates configuration classes at build "
"time based on annotations on your registrar provider."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Custom Service Registrar Provider"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Stork uses a provider model.\n"
"To create a custom registrar, you need two classes:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A *provider* implementing `ServiceRegistrarProvider` — the factory that "
"creates registrar instances."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A *registrar* implementing `ServiceRegistrar` — the actual registration "
"logic."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Let's start with the provider.\n"
"Create the `src/main/java/org/acme/services/CustomServiceRegistrarProvider."
"java` file with the following content:"
msgstr ""

msgid "There are a few important things to note:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@ServiceRegistrarType` annotation declares the registrar _type_.\n"
"This is the value used in the `quarkus.stork.<service-name>.service-"
"registrar.type` property.\n"
"Here, it is `custom`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@ServiceRegistrarAttribute` annotations declare the configuration "
"attributes for this registrar.\n"
"Stork's annotation processor (provided by `stork-configuration-generator`) "
"uses these annotations to generate\n"
"the `CustomRegistrarConfiguration` class at compile time. You do not need to "
"write this class yourself."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@ApplicationScoped` annotation makes this provider a CDI bean, so Stork "
"can discover it automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `createServiceRegistrar` method is the factory that creates a "
"`CustomServiceRegistrar` from the generated configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Custom Service Registrar"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now let's implement the registrar itself.\n"
"Create the `src/main/java/org/acme/services/CustomServiceRegistrar.java` "
"file with the following content:"
msgstr ""

msgid "This registrar:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Receives its configuration (host and port) from the generated "
"`CustomRegistrarConfiguration` class."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stores registered instances in a `ConcurrentHashMap`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Implements `registerServiceInstance` to add a service instance to the map."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Implements `deregisterServiceInstance` to remove a service instance on "
"shutdown."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Both methods return `Uni<Void>`, since Stork uses Mutiny for reactive "
"support."
msgstr ""

msgid "Programmatic Service Registration at Startup"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With the registrar in place, we can now register service instances "
"programmatically.\n"
"Create the `src/main/java/org/acme/services/Registration.java` file with the "
"following content:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the application starts, this CDI bean observes the `StartupEvent` and "
"uses the Stork API to register a service instance.\n"
"The `Stork.getInstance().getService(\"my-service\")` call retrieves the "
"Stork service named `my-service`, and `registerInstance`\n"
"delegates to the custom registrar we created earlier."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stork configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid "Now we need to configure Stork to use our custom registrar."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the `src/main/resources/application.properties`, add:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus.stork.my-service.service-registrar.type` property tells Stork "
"to use the `custom` registrar type.\n"
"This matches the value declared in the `@ServiceRegistrarType` annotation on "
"`CustomServiceRegistrarProvider`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus.stork.my-service.service-registrar.host` property maps to the "
"`host` attribute declared with `@ServiceRegistrarAttribute` on the provider.\n"
"This is a required attribute."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can optionally set `quarkus.stork.my-service.service-registrar.port` as "
"well, since the provider declares an optional `port` attribute.\n"
"If omitted, the registrar defaults to port `8080`."
msgstr ""

